  "about": "app-reset at 1.25, on the ThinkPad's display (1600x1000): the same steps, the same answers. Resetting an application (docs/adr/0061-crashes-and-resetting-an-application.mdx, decision 5): Crash Probe, installed, quits at every launch because its storage file in the run's home is corrupt. Opened from the dock and reopened from its notification, it quits twice: the sheet. Its Reset… asks the session, which asks the person in its own sheet what is erased and what is kept; Cancel erases nothing. Opened again from the dock it quits again: the sheet; Reset… and Reset: the session erases its data and cache directories, and nothing else of the home (a note, another application's data), and opens it again, as new: it reads nothing, counts its first launch and says it is ready. With the session erasing before it asks, or erasing more than the application's own, the run fails.",
